      "comment" : "A choice of the Reading List's When a book ends pop-up button: when a book opened from the list ends, stop there.\nButton of the Compare Libraries sheet that stops the comparison.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Detener"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Stop At" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the sleep timer sheet's section of timers that stop at a place in the book: End of heading and End of book.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Detener en"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Stop Comparing" : {
      "comment" : "Button in Storage settings that stops the comparison made before Use This Library."
    },
    "Stop at the end of the book" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the sleep timer sheet's End of book button, which sets a timer that stops where the book ends.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Detener al final del libro"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Stop at the end of this heading" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the sleep timer sheet's End of heading button, which sets a timer that stops where the heading playing ends.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Detener al final de este encabezado"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Stops comparing. Nothing in either copy has been changed." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Stop button of the Compare Libraries sheet."
    },
    "Stops saying the code was guessed. The book is not read again." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts."
    },
    "Subfolders" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Folder Settings sheet, which shows one library folder's facts and its listening options. The label of the folder's own subfolders, shown only when it has any."
    },
    "Subscribed" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. A condition's relation as its relation pop-up names it, by its test and whether it is negated. This is the form for the other case of the condition."
    },
    "Subscription" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. A kind of test as a condition's test pop-up names it. This is the case .subscribed."
    },
    "Takes %lld to %lld minutes." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the sleep timer sheet's custom minutes field on the iPhone: the fewest and most minutes it takes. %1$lld is the fewest (1); %2$lld the most (480).",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Takes %1$lld to %2$lld minutes."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Admite de %1$lld a %2$lld minutos."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Takes %lld to %lld minutes. Return sets the timer and plays the book." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the sleep timer sheet's custom minutes field on the Mac: the fewest and most minutes it takes, and what the Return key does there. %1$lld is the fewest (1); %2$lld the most (480). Return is the name of the key.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Takes %1$lld to %2$lld minutes. Return sets the timer and plays the book."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Admite de %1$lld a %2$lld minutos. Retorno programa el temporizador y reproduce el libro."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Takes each finished book off the list when its window moves on or closes. Books finished before you turn it on stay." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Reading List's Remove books when finished checkbox.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Quita de la lista cada libro terminado cuando su ventana pasa a otro libro o se cierra. Los libros terminados antes de activarlo se quedan."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Takes the selected books off the reading list. They stay in the library." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Library's edit-mode bar button Remove from Reading List.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Quita los libros seleccionados de la lista de lectura. Siguen en la biblioteca."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Text Encoding" : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. The label of Book Information's row, and pop-up, that names the encoding."
    },
    "Text encoding: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Speak Info's sentence for an encoding described as description (\"Windows-1251 (Cyrillic), guessed\"): \"Text encoding: Windows-1251 (Cyrillic), guessed\". Placeholders in order: description."
    },
    "TextMouth closed while opening %@, so it wasn't reopened." : {
      "comment" : "Announced at launch after the app closed while it was opening a book. %@ is the book's title, which is not opened again."
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't keep the text you changed in “%@” beside the new reading, so it left the book as it was." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Why the book titled bookTitle was not read again: the text changed with Edit Text could not be kept beside the new reading, so nothing was replaced, as Replace Existing leaves both copies then (DuplicateReplacement.TextNotKept). Placeholders in order: bookTitle."
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't read %lld files, so this may be incomplete." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of Use This Library's account: some files could not be read. %lld is how many files, a count.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth couldn't read %lld file, so this may be incomplete."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth couldn't read %lld files, so this may be incomplete."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't read “%@” again, so it left the book as it was." : {
      "comment" : "Why a book was not read again with another encoding or braille code: the reading failed. %@ is the book's title."
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't read “%@” again, so it left the book as it was: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Why a book was not read again with another encoding or braille code: the reading failed. %1$@ is the book's title and %2$@ is the reason in English, as the reader worded it.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth couldn't read “%1$@” again, so it left the book as it was: %2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't tell which copy is newer (%@)." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of Use This Library's account when the comparison could not be made. %@ is the reason in English."
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't tell which copy is newer." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of Use This Library's account when the comparison could not be made and no reason is known."
    },
    "TextMouth is not downloading right now." : {
      "comment" : "Why the download of a feed's next episode did not start: the app is quitting or the feed is being deleted. Said after \"The next episode could not be downloaded, so playback stopped.\"",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no está descargando en este momento."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is reading the library's text again. Try again when that finishes." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Why a book can't be read again while the library's text is being read again (the launch batch, Redo Text Extraction), in the words TextMouth uses while its storage work is held (StorageBusyError)."
    },
    "TextMouth is reading “%@” again in another encoding. Try again when that finishes." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Why what would rewrite the text of the book titled bookTitle waits while TextMouth reads it again in another encoding, in the same words as extractionRefusal: a second re-read of it, Edit Text, Redo Text Extraction, and Replace Existing (LibraryViewModel.readingAgainRefusal(of:)). Placeholders in order: bookTitle."
    },
    "TextMouth is reading “%@” again with another braille code. Try again when that finishes." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Why what would rewrite the text of the braille book titled bookTitle waits while TextMouth reads it again with another braille code, as the other re-reads' sentences say it (TextEncodingWording.readingAgainRefusal(bookTitle:), BrailleFileCodeWording.readingAgainRefusal(bookTitle:)). Placeholders in order: bookTitle."
    },
    "TextMouth is reading “%@” again with other braille file characters. Try again when that finishes." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Why what would rewrite the text of the braille book titled bookTitle waits while TextMouth reads it again with other braille file characters, as the encoding's sentence says it for any other book (TextEncodingWording.readingAgainRefusal(bookTitle:)): a second re-read of it, Edit Text, Redo Text Extraction, and Replace Existing (LibraryViewModel.readingAgainRefusal(of:)). Placeholders in order: bookTitle."
    },
    "TextMouth reads its file as it reads a file you add: in the encoding the file names, or else the one TextMouth finds." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. What Automatic does, as the alert says it before it is chosen."
    },
    "The %@ of %lld of them are kept." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence that says what is kept of some of several deleted downloads. %1$@ is a list of parts, such as \"places and bookmarks\", and %2$lld is how many of the downloads keep them, a count.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "The %@ of %lld of them are kept."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "The %@ of %lld of them are kept."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The %lld selected books are already in the reading list." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver announcement when Add to Reading List added nothing: every book selected is on the list already. %lld is the number of books selected (two or more).",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Los %lld libros seleccionados ya están en la lista de lectura."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Library holds at most %lld views." : {
      "comment" : "Hint of New View and Duplicate in the Library tab of Settings when the limit is reached, and the problem Save reports there. %lld is the most views the Library holds, a count.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
