    },
    "The view is first in the list." : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library tab of Settings, a list of the views the Library window offers (built-in views and the listener's own). Move Up's hint while the view is first, when it is dimmed."
    },
    "The view is last in the list." : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library tab of Settings, a list of the views the Library window offers (built-in views and the listener's own). Move Down's hint while the view is last, when it is dimmed."
    },
    "The view this window showed was deleted. It now shows %@." : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library window's View pop-up and Go to View. What a window announces when the view it showed was deleted, from Settings or by a change of config.json, and it shows name, the first view its pop-up offers, instead. Placeholders in order: name."
    },
    "Their %@ are kept." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence that says what is kept of every one of several deleted downloads. %@ is a list of parts, such as \"places and bookmarks\"."
    },
    "Their places, bookmarks, and transcripts, if they have any, are kept, and they can be downloaded again." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence about several deleted downloads: what the listener left in them is kept, and they can be downloaded again."
    },
    "There is no view %@. Go to View reaches %lld views." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver announcement when a Go to View key has no view. %1$@ is the view's number as the listener pressed it, an identifier written without digit grouping. %2$lld is how many views Go to View reaches, a count.",
